trait RangePhaseSeal {}
/// Which form a generated carrier's leaves take: the RANGE AXIS of its type.
///
/// Every generated carrier struct and choice enum is written ONCE, with a
/// parameter `R: RangePhase<'tree> = Raw`, and every leaf and container of its
/// fields is spelled through `R`'s projections. The two phases are the only
/// implementations, and the trait is sealed so no third can be added:
///
/// | projection | [`Raw`] | [`Ranged<'source>`](Ranged) |
/// |---|---|---|
/// | `Wrapper<W>` | `W` | [`SourceBound<'tree, 'source, W>`](SourceBound) |
/// | `KindMissing<T>` | [`KindMissing<T>`] | `T` |
/// | `Node` | `tree_sitter::Node<'tree>` | [`SourceSlice<'tree, 'source>`](SourceSlice) |
/// | `Extra` | [`Extra<'tree>`](Extra) | [`SourceSlice<'tree, 'source>`](SourceSlice) |
/// | `LeafText` | [`LeafText<'tree>`](LeafText) | [`SourceSlice<'tree, 'source>`](SourceSlice) |
/// | `LeafSpan` | [`LeafSpan<'tree>`](LeafSpan) | [`ReadableLeafSpan<'tree, 'source>`](ReadableLeafSpan) |
/// | `Slot<T, M, U, A>` | [`NodeSlot`] | [`ReadableSlot`] |
/// | `Positioned<S>` | [`Positioned`] | [`ReadablePositioned`] |
///
/// The phase is a TYPE, not a flag. Extraction produces only `Raw` carriers,
/// and the one route from a `Raw` carrier to its `Ranged` form is
/// [`SourceChildren::admit_ranges`], which consumes it and checks every
/// selected leaf range on the way. A `Ranged` carrier has no admission of its
/// own, so it cannot be admitted twice, and a `Raw` one cannot be read as if
/// its ranges had been checked. Carrier fields are public, so a `Ranged`
/// value can also be assembled by hand; what certifies its leaves is then
/// each leaf's own type ([`SourceBound`], [`SourceSlice`]), whose constructors
/// are private to the producer, not the carrier.
///
/// Each leaf's [`AdmitRanges::Admitted`] (the runtime leaves here, and every
/// generated wrapper) is DEFINED as the `Ranged` projection above, so the
/// table has one owner and the structural admission of a generated carrier
/// type-checks only because the two agree.
#[allow(private_bounds)]
pub trait RangePhase<'tree>: RangePhaseSeal {
    /// A typed node wrapper.
    type Wrapper<W: SourceBoundKind<'tree>>;
    /// The payload of a kind-proven MISSING placeholder whose present form is `T`.
    type KindMissing<T>;
    /// A raw node: an untyped partial, a recovery node or an unexpected child.
    type Node;
    /// A skippable extra.
    type Extra;
    /// An absorbed-anonymous leaf's own span.
    type LeafText;
    /// An absorbed-anonymous inter-sibling sub-span.
    type LeafSpan;
    /// A position's five states, narrowed by the payload parameters.
    type Slot<T, M, E, U, A>;
    /// A slot or collection with its leading extras.
    type Positioned<S>;
}
